1112,92,382,32,12671,315,10578,400,17,3,374,1640,17433,304,264,5234,292,7074,11,438,6839,13,576,3082,4766,279,5234,292,7074,714,4889,279,12671,374,91766,13,3555,19419,315,279,5234,292,7074,594,3082,374,91766,1939,58,6405,921,25643,551,7,21,3821,317,2258,2752,2333,258,28357,14618,23,417,7257,45801,7,23,417,1106,16119,37591,28,19,401,7559,7633,4346,1287,1188,15,11,15,701,19,11,15,11,16,23,15,29621,21621,11,11650,11,11453,317,7559,7633,3025,7074,1188,15,11,17,701,17,701,5782,11,11453,317,16119,1188,15,11,17,1106,7633,1188,15,11,17,29621,1188,15,11,17,7257,17,9,3741,7,21,15,4945,1502,20912,17,73315,16106,2768,1188,15,11,17,29621,1188,15,11,17,7257,17,9,3741,7,21,15,36363,925,317,24157,6405,60,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nA circle of radius $2$ is inscribed in a semicircle, as shown. The area inside the semicircle but outside the circle is shaded. What fraction of the semicircle's area is shaded?\n\n[asy]\nunitsize(6mm);\ndefaultpen(linewidth(.8pt)+fontsize(8pt));\ndotfactor=4;\n\nfilldraw(Arc((0,0),4,0,180)--cycle,gray,black);\nfilldraw(Circle((0,2),2),white,black);\ndot((0,2));\ndraw((0,2)--((0,2)+2*dir(60)));\nlabel(\"$2$\",midpoint((0,2)--((0,2)+2*dir(60))),SE);\n[/asy]","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"9ca08233c361238d972f9b0c0d8ee547c2857c0d0f6fc9e5a5d137d362153f62"},"seconds":13.036014556884766,"seed":219347564625841500,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to find the fraction of the semicircle's area that is shaded. This involves calculating the area of the semicircle and the area of the inscribed circle, then finding the difference between these areas.\n\n### Step 1: Calculate the Area of the Semicircle\nThe radius of the semicircle is given as 4. The area \\(A_{\\text{semicircle}}\\) of a full circle with radius \\(r\\) is given by the formula:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{circle}} = \\pi r^2\n\\]\nFor a semicircle, the area is half of this:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{semicircle}} = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi r^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi (4)^2 = \\frac{1}{2} \\pi \\cdot 16 = 8\\pi\n\\]\n\n### Step 2: Calculate the Area of the Inscribed Circle\nThe radius of the inscribed circle is given as 2. The area \\(A_{\\text{circle}}\\) of a full circle with radius \\(r\\) is:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{circle}} = \\pi r^2\n\\]\nFor the inscribed circle, the area is:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{inscribed circle}} = \\pi (2)^2 = \\pi \\cdot 4 = 4\\pi\n\\]\n\n### Step 3: Calculate the Shaded Area\nThe shaded area is the area of the semicircle minus the area of the inscribed circle:\n\\[\nA_{\\text{shaded}} = A_{\\text{semicircle}} - A_{\\text{inscribed circle}} = 8\\pi - 4\\pi = 4\\pi\n\\]\n\n### Step 4: Determine the Fraction of the Semicircle's Area that is Shaded\nThe fraction of the semicircle's area that is shaded is the shaded area divided by the area of the semicircle:\n\\[\n\\text{Fraction shaded} = \\frac{A_{\\text{shaded}}}{A_{\\text{semicircle}}} = \\frac{4\\pi}{8\\pi} = \\frac{4}{8} = \\frac{1}{2}\n\\]\n\nThus, the fraction of the semicircle's area that is shaded is:\n\\[\n\\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}\n\\]"},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{\\frac{1}{2}}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"prealgebra:6"}
